# Male (one thread per male body)
# hardware/male/__init__.py - owns Drives, Search (which owns Blink), turn_back_and_forth, neopixels, 4 light sensors. Started by Hardware.setup() - never started on its own by anything else. Drives and Search are expanded inline below, each at the point it actually starts.

0 setup(): dxl.init_hardware(), then starts Drives (started_by=self). Both O and P drives begin counting from their configured start values
-> thread-drives-male
0 loop(): if search is already started, do nothing this tick
0 loop(): else if not is_satisfied() (neither drive is freshly satisfied), start search (started_by=self). This can happen on the very first tick if the male's configured start values are already above the satisfaction limit
-> thread-search-male
0 repeats every ~10ms tick, doing nothing once search has started
0 setdown(): stops Drives, stops Search - this is the only thing that ever stops a running Search (SCENARIOS.md 1.2)
